from science_completion import q,p,m
QUESTIONS=[
q(1,'Convert 30 cm³ into dm³.','0.030 dm³.','MS1a;WS4.5'),q(1,'Write 0.0006 in standard form.','6 ×10⁻⁴.','MS1b'),q(1,'How many significant figures are in 0.00480?','Three.','MS2a'),q(1,'What does an element’s atomic number count?','Protons.','Appendix A;4.1.1.4'),q(1,'What is the chemical symbol for potassium?','K.','4.1.1.1'),q(1,'What is the chemical symbol for iron?','Fe.','4.1.1.1'),q(1,'What unit is used for the quantity of substance?','Mole, mol.','4.3.2.1'),q(1,'What volume does one mole of gas occupy at room temperature and pressure in the course approximation?','24 dm³.','4.3.5'),q(1,'What does ∝ mean?','Proportional to.','MS3a'),q(1,'Which graph feature gives instantaneous reaction rate?','Tangent gradient.','MS4e'),
q(2,'Convert 0.0025 kg to grams and 500 cm³ to dm³.','- 0.0025 ×1000 = **2.5 g**.\n- 500/1000 = **0.500 dm³**.','WS4.5'),
q(2,'Calculate (8 ×10⁴)/(2 ×10²).','- 8/2 =4; exponent =4−2 =2.\n- **4 ×10²**.','MS1b'),
q(2,'Round 0.04682 to three significant figures.','- Count from the first non-zero digit, 4.\n- **0.0468**.','MS2a'),
q(2,'A quantity rises from 80 to 100. Calculate percentage increase.','- (100−80)/80 ×100.\n- **25%**.','MS1c'),
q(2,'Determine protons and electrons in Mg²⁺, atomic number 12.','- **12 protons**.\n- **10 electrons**, after losing two.','Appendix A;4.1.1.4'),
q(2,'An isotope has atomic number 17 and mass number 37. Find neutron count and explain why decimal Ar is not used.','- Neutrons =37−17 = **20**.\n- Ar is a weighted isotope mean, not this individual isotope’s mass number.','4.1.1.4;4.1.1.6'),
q(2,'Write the formula formed by Al³⁺ and O²⁻.','- Equal charges require two aluminium ions (+6) and three oxide ions (−6).\n- **Al₂O₃**.','4.1.1.1'),
q(2,'Write the formula formed by Ca²⁺ and NO₃⁻.','- Two nitrate ions balance one calcium ion.\n- **Ca(NO₃)₂**, retaining the nitrate group.','4.1.1.1'),
q(2,'Calculate Mr of Mg(OH)₂ using Mg=24, O=16 and H=1.','- 24+2×(16+1).\n- **58**, with no unit on Mr.','4.3.1.2'),
q(2,'Calculate moles in 7.2 g magnesium, Ar=24.','- n =7.2/24.\n- **0.30 mol**.','4.3.2.1'),
q(2,'Calculate mass of 0.15 mol carbon dioxide, Mr=44.','- Mass =0.15 ×44.\n- **6.6 g**.','4.3.2.1'),
q(2,'Calculate moles in 240 cm³ gas at room temperature and pressure.','- n =240/24 000.\n- **0.010 mol**.','4.3.5'),
q(2,'Calculate mass concentration for 3.0 g solute in 200 cm³ solution.','- Volume = **0.200 dm³**.\n- Concentration =3.0/0.200 = **15 g dm⁻³**.','4.3.2.5'),
q(2,'Calculate percentage yield from actual 6.0 g and theoretical 8.0 g.','- 6.0/8.0 ×100.\n- **75%**.','4.3.3.1'),
q(2,'Calculate Rf from spot distance 18 mm and front distance 30 mm.','- 18/30.\n- **0.60**, no unit.','4.8.1.3'),
q(2,'Rearrange c=n/V to make V the subject.','- Multiply by V: cV=n.\n- Divide by c: **V=n/c**.','MS3b'),
q(3,'Calculate weighted Ar for 80% isotope mass 10 and 20% isotope mass 11.','- Weighted total =80×10 +20×11 = **1020**.\n- Divide by100.\n- **Ar =10.2**; individual atoms still have integer mass numbers.','4.1.1.6'),
q(3,'Calculate nitrogen’s mass percentage in NH₄NO₃, using N=14, H=1, O=16.','- Mr =2×14 +4×1 +3×16 = **80**.\n- Nitrogen contribution = **28**.\n- Percentage =28/80 ×100 = **35%**.','4.3.1.2','2023 2H Q05.2: adapted element-percentage method'),
q(3,'Calculate the number of molecules in 0.20 mol H₂ using 6.02 ×10²³ mol⁻¹, and the number of H atoms.','- Molecules =0.20 ×6.02 ×10²³ = **1.204 ×10²³**.\n- Each molecule contains two atoms.\n- H atoms = **2.408 ×10²³** before final requested rounding.','4.3.2.1'),
q(3,'For 2Mg+O₂ →2MgO, find oxygen moles and MgO mass from 0.10 mol Mg; MgO Mr=40.','- Oxygen needed =0.10/2 = **0.050 mol**.\n- MgO formed = **0.10 mol**.\n- Mass =0.10 ×40 = **4.0 g**, if reaction completes with enough oxygen.','4.3.2.2'),
q(3,'Find empirical formula from 2.4 g carbon and 0.6 g hydrogen; Ar values 12 and 1.','- Carbon moles =2.4/12 = **0.20**. Hydrogen moles =0.6/1 = **0.60**.\n- Divide by0.20: ratio **1:3**.\n- Empirical formula **CH₃**.','4.3.2'),
q(3,'An empirical formula is CH₂ and molecular Mr is 56. Determine molecular formula.','- Empirical mass =12+2 = **14**.\n- Multiplier =56/14 = **4**.\n- Molecular formula **C₄H₈**.','4.3.2'),
q(3,'Calculate molar concentration of 2.0 g NaOH in 250 cm³; Mr=40.','- Moles =2.0/40 = **0.050 mol**.\n- Volume = **0.250 dm³**.\n- c =0.050/0.250 = **0.200 mol dm⁻³** before rounding to requested precision.','4.3.4'),
q(3,'Convert 0.25 mol dm⁻³ sodium carbonate to g dm⁻³, using Na=23, C=12 and O=16.','- Mr(Na₂CO₃)=46+12+48 = **106**.\n- Mass concentration =0.25 ×106.\n- **26.5 g dm⁻³**, before final requested rounding.','4.3.4'),
q(3,'Calculate atom economy for CaCO₃ →CaO+CO₂ when CaO is desired; masses 100, 56 and 44.','- Desired contribution = **56**.\n- Total product contribution =56+44 = **100**.\n- Atom economy =56/100 ×100 = **56%**.','4.3.3.2'),
q(3,'A tangent has points (10 s, 8 cm³) and (50 s, 32 cm³). Calculate instantaneous rate.','- ΔV =32−8 = **24 cm³**.\n- Δt =50−10 = **40 s**.\n- Rate =24/40 = **0.60 cm³ s⁻¹**.','MS4e;4.6.1.1','2023 2H Q07.3: adapted tangent method'),
q(3,'A line passes through (2, 7) and (8, 19). Find gradient and intercept.','- m =(19−7)/(8−2)= **2**.\n- 7=2×2+c, so **c=3**.\n- y= **2x+3**.','MS4b;MS4d'),
q(3,'Measurements 18.9, 19.0 and 19.1 cm³ are concordant. Calculate their mean and range.','- Mean =(18.9+19.0+19.1)/3 = **19.0 cm³**.\n- Range =19.1−18.9 = **0.2 cm³**.\n- Report precision consistently with the measurement resolution.','MS2b;WS3.4'),
q(3,'Counts 1, 2 and 3 have frequencies 2, 5 and 3. Calculate the mean count.','- Weighted total =1×2 +2×5 +3×3 = **21**.\n- Total frequency = **10**.\n- Mean =21/10 = **2.1**.','MS2c'),
q(3,'Calculate surface area and volume of a cube with side 2 cm.','- Surface =6×2² = **24 cm²**.\n- Volume =2³ = **8 cm³**.\n- SA:V =24:8 = **3:1**.','MS5c'),
q(4,'For 2Mg+O₂ →2MgO, a mixture has 0.30 mol Mg and 0.10 mol O₂. Identify limiting reagent and amounts left/formed.','- Compare moles/coefficient: Mg 0.30/2=0.15; oxygen 0.10/1=0.10.\n- **Oxygen limits**.\n- It uses **0.20 mol Mg**, leaving **0.10 mol Mg**.\n- Forms **0.20 mol MgO**.','4.3.2.4'),
q(4,'A 25.0 cm³ NaOH sample requires 15.0 cm³ of 0.100 mol dm⁻³ H₂SO₄. Calculate NaOH concentration.','- Acid moles =0.100×0.0150 = **0.00150 mol**.\n- H₂SO₄+2NaOH →Na₂SO₄+2H₂O gives 1:2 ratio.\n- NaOH moles = **0.00300 mol**.\n- c =0.00300/0.0250 = **0.120 mol dm⁻³**.','4.3.4;RPA2'),
q(4,'Use H–H436, Cl–Cl243 and H–Cl431 kJ mol⁻¹ to calculate energy change for H₂+Cl₂ →2HCl.','- Broken bonds:436+243 = **679 kJ mol⁻¹**.\n- Formed bonds:2×431 = **862 kJ mol⁻¹**.\n- Change =679−862 = **−183 kJ mol⁻¹**.\n- Negative means **exothermic**, for the reaction quantities shown.','4.5.1.3'),
q(4,'A 2 cm cube is cut into eight 1 cm cubes. Compare total volume and exposed surface area.','- Original volume = **8 cm³** and surface = **24 cm²**.\n- New total volume =8×1 = **8 cm³**, unchanged.\n- New total surface =8×6 = **48 cm²**, doubled.\n- More exposed area can increase solid reaction rate without adding substance.','MS5c;4.6.1.3'),
q(4,'Explain how to extract a rate from a curved chemical graph without confusing it with yield.','- Draw tangent at the specified time.\n- Calculate Δquantity/Δtime on a large triangle using actual scales.\n- Give correct rate units.\n- Final curve height measures total amount, not instantaneous speed.','MS4e'),
q(4,'Using the same temperature and pressure, determine oxygen needed for 120 cm³ hydrogen in 2H₂+O₂ →2H₂O, and hydrogen moles at room conditions.','- Gas-volume ratio H₂:O₂ = **2:1**.\n- Oxygen required =120/2 = **60 cm³**.\n- Hydrogen moles =120/24 000.\n- **0.0050 mol**.','4.3.5'),
q(4,'A 10 g 18-carat gold alloy is recycled with 90% of its gold recovered. Calculate gold content and recovery.','- Gold fraction =18/24 = **0.75**.\n- Original gold =10×0.75 = **7.5 g**.\n- Recovery =7.5×0.90.\n- **6.75 g gold**, before rounding to requested precision.','4.10.3.2;MS1c'),
q(4,'A gas-production rate rises linearly from 0 to 8 cm³ s⁻¹ over 5 seconds. Calculate gas produced from the rate-time graph.','- Total amount is the **area under the rate-time graph**.\n- Triangle area =½×5×8.\n- Result = **20**.\n- Units s×cm³ s⁻¹ give **20 cm³**.','WS3.3;MS5c')]
